[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi all, sharing a Lean 4 + Mathlib formalization of the generalized Fermat equation x² + y⁵ = z⁷: no solutions in nonzero coprime integers.</p>\n<p>The main statements are in <code>Challenge.lean</code>, which only imports Mathlib. Comparator checks the proofs against it, using Lean's kernel, NanoDa and con-ron. It's about 29,000 lines, standard axioms only, no <code>sorry</code> and no <code>native_decide</code>.</p>\n<p>It assumes two things: Putz's classification theorem, and a class-group condition that the paper proves by computation (that part isn't formalized).</p>\n<p>The paper, the proof and the formalization were all done by a multi-agent AI system I built.</p>\n<p>Repo: <a href=\"https://github.com/manvirjaswal/generalized-fermat-257-lean\">https://github.com/manvirjaswal/generalized-fermat-257-lean</a><br>\nPaper: <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23223027\">https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23223027</a></p>",
        "id": 630275236,
        "sender_full_name": "Manvir Jaswal",
        "timestamp": 1791496461
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Palomar: <a href=\"https://palomar-registry.org/entry?id=PALOMAR-2026-10-09-000002&amp;version=1\">https://palomar-registry.org/entry?id=PALOMAR-2026-10-09-000002&amp;version=1</a></p>",
        "id": 630314844,
        "sender_full_name": "Manvir Jaswal",
        "timestamp": 1791517320
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>To save everyone a click, here's the main theorem:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- **Theorem 1.2**, the equivalent form: under the same hypotheses, `x⁵ + y⁷ = z²` has no solution</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">in nonzero integers with `gcd(x, y, z) = 1`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">theorem_1_2_572</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hPutz</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">gcd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">gcd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">7</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">AdjoinRoot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fpoly</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℚ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℚ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">7</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃ₐ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ℚ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L8</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hclass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ClassGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">𝓞</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L24</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hz</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">gcd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">gcd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">7</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Personally, I think this result would be much more convincing if you are able to remove the assumptions <code>hPutz</code> and <code>hclass</code> since it is not obvious to me that these axioms are correct.</p>",
        "id": 630675042,
        "sender_full_name": "Jack McCarthy",
        "timestamp": 1791667707
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi Jack, thanks for the feedback.</p>\n<p>I looked into removing both, but each is too large a project for me right now. <code>hPutz</code> is Putz’s Theorem 4.33, which rests on Magma computations (local computations and elliptic-curve Chabauty) that would all have to be redone. <code>hclass</code> is proved in the paper without GRH (Appendix B), but formalizing it would need Weil’s explicit formula, which isn’t in Mathlib yet.</p>\n<p>Theorem 1.1, that no solution has fibre isomorphic to Putz’s field L₈, uses only <code>hclass</code>.</p>",
        "id": 630677709,
        "sender_full_name": "Manvir Jaswal",
        "timestamp": 1791669673
    }
]